  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nThe low pressure that brought widespread rain to our area has \nmoved east. Looking at dry, but slightly cooler than normal \ntemps through the weekend. Models continue to show a trough of \nlow pressure arriving Monday night into Tuesday. QPF with this \nsystem is up to 0.25 inches for the mountains and highlands but \nonly a few hundredths fro the Snake River Plain into the Magic \nValley. We could see some light snow above 6500 feet with this \nsystem, with early amounts ranging between 1 and 3 inches. This \ndoes look like a breezy system with the NBM already advertising \nwind gusts to 30 mph. Temperatures for the remainder of the week\nshould be near or slightly below average. Perhaps another weak \nsystem arriving for late next week.",
